-- title:
--   Order of the Hasse radicand at supersingular places is ≡ 1 mod (p-1)
-- statement:
--   Let $p \ge 5$ be a prime and let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$; let $M \ge 5$ be a nonzero natural number with $p \nmid M$. Let $w$ be an integral weight-one form of level $M$ over $\kappa$, i.e. a weight-one modular form for $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with a power series over $\mathbb Z$ whose image in $\mathbb C[[q]]$ is its $q$-expansion and whose reduction $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\ \kappa\ w.\mathrm{series}$ in $\kappa[[q]] \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \kappa$ is nonzero. Let $m, e_4, e_6 \in \mathbb N$ and $S \in \kappa[X]$ satisfy $12m + 4e_4 + 6e_6 = p-1$, $e_4 \le 1$, $e_6 \le 1$, with $S$ monic and separable of degree $m$, $S(0) \ne 0$, $S(1728) \ne 0$, and the identity $\theta(\bar\jmath)^{(p-1)/2}\, S(\bar\jmath) = (-1)^{(p-1)/2}\,\bar\jmath^{\,4m+e_4+2e_6}(\bar\jmath - 1728)^{3m+e_4+e_6}$ in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \kappa$, where $\bar\jmath = \mathrm{jqModC}\ \kappa$ is $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $\kappa$ of the integral power series $\mathrm{jNum} = E_4^3 \cdot \eta^{-24}$-numerator, and $\theta$ is the derivation $f \mapsto q\,\mathrm{d}f/\mathrm{d}q$ on Laurent series. Let $F = \mathrm{x1FunctionFieldC}\ \kappa\ M$ be the $\kappa$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \kappa$ generated by the ratios of integral forms for $\Gamma_1(M)$, let $J \in F$ have $q$-expansion $\bar\jmath$, and let $b \in F$ have $q$-expansion $(\mathrm{intSeriesC}\ \kappa\ w.\mathrm{series})^{-(p-1)}$. Let $x$ be a place of $F$ over $\kappa$ (a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $\kappa$ and a principal ideal ring), with associated order function $\mathrm{ord}_x$, and let $j_0 \in \kappa$ satisfy $\mathrm{ord}_x(J - j_0) \ge 1$ and $j_0^{e_4}(j_0 - 1728)^{e_6} S(j_0) = 0$. Then $p - 1$ divides $\mathrm{ord}_x(b) - 1$ in $\mathbb Z$.
--
--   This records the behaviour of the radicand of the Hasse invariant, written in the $q$-expansion function field of $X_1(M)$ over $\kappa$, at a place lying over a supersingular $j$-invariant: the Hasse invariant has simple zeros at the supersingular points, so the order of $b$ is congruent to $1$ modulo $p-1$ rather than equal to $1$, the discrepancy being $(p-1)\,\mathrm{ord}_x$ of the reduced weight-one form. It is used in the computation of $\gcd(p-1, |\mathrm{ord}_x b|)$ at supersingular places, and rests on the Deuring–Igusa factorisation of the supersingular polynomial, the divisibility by $12$ of the order of $w^{12}/\Delta$ at affine places, and the identification of $\mathrm{ord}_x(J - j_0)$ with the ramification index $\mathrm{jWidth}(j_0) \in \{1,2,3\}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_sub_one_dvd_ord_sub_one_of_coe_eq_hasseRootFn_pow_of_eval_eq_zero.lean

